Z||000000||mikabika||08-31-2001||01:25 PM||||I want to do something to my Fiero GT, This is the hardest thing ever!! I want to put a plain white ball shifter knob on my 5-speed.<BR>All I hear from everone from Hurst Shifters, to every part store punk in town, is "It can't be done!" So just remember guys,please don't try this at home, no one will ever get it to work!!!! &lt;grin&gt;||||reg||8
Z||000001||Formula88||08-31-2001||01:29 PM||||Well, the problem is our shifter is 16mm diameter.  Most aftermarket knobs are smaller than that.  The lever is threaded for M16x1.5 (16mm diameter, 1.5mm pitch) - so anything with that threading will fit.  Try asking for that instead of a "Fiero" shift knob and see if you have any luck.||||reg||4
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||08-31-2001||01:31 PM||||cant be done?<P>techically anything can be done<P>its only a matter of time, money, and people to do the work.<P>Whatever shape the end of the shifter lever is, if you remove or cut the handle off, and make the same shaped hole in your white ball, get some epoxy...<P>whats the big deal?! you could glue a bowling ball on there if you wanted to.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||08-31-2001||01:33 PM||||havent these guys ever heard of a drill press?<P>or a tap?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||08-31-2001||01:58 PM||||When I installed my Autozone special shift knob I just cut the old bent rod out and welded in a 5/16 bolt instead.||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||08-31-2001||02:24 PM||||MOMO Corse, isotta, and Rimmer all have differnt weighted shift "knobs" that will work... availible at <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  and options auto salon not sure of their web address. been tere.. I worked at NOPI. i know they fit.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstmeatsig.jpg">          <BR>www.engineered.net||||reg||1
